First, let's figure out how many potatoes the chef still needs to cook. He needs 12 potatoes and has already cooked 6, so he needs to cook 12 - 6 = 6 potatoes.

Each potato takes 6 minutes to cook, so 6 potatoes will take 6 potatoes * 6 minutes/potato = 36 minutes.

\boxed{36}

Oliver starts with 33 dollars. In January, he still has 33 dollars. In March, he spent 4 dollars, so he has 33 - 4 = 29 dollars. Then he got 32 dollars from his mom, so he has 29 + 32 = 61 dollars.

Therefore, Oliver has 61 dollars.

\boxed{61}
